<title>CANADA: Toronto stocks gain one percent as golds rise.</title>
<headline>Toronto stocks gain one percent as golds rise.</headline>
<text>
<p>CHANGE				    CHANGE</p>
<p>TSE	 6229.52   +72.05   HI 6222.52	    LO  6191.00</p>
<p>DJI	 7169.94   +32.92   GOLD (LONDON)   US$345.85 +4.75</p>
<p>FTSE100   4630.90   +50.50   GOLD (NY-COMEX) US$349.30 +4.50</p>
<p>NIKKEI   19802.78  -259.03   LME CASH NICKEL US$7680   +50.0</p>
<p>CANDLR     1.3915		LME CASH ALUM   US$1648.5 +42.0</p>
<p>CAN 30-YR  110.80    +0.90   BRENT CRUDE     US$18.94  +0.25</p>
<p>--------------------MARKET COMMENT----------------------------</p>
<p>* Toronto stocks jumped almost 1.2 percent on Friday, driven by a dramatic rise in golds as bullion prices improved. * 17 million shares traded worth C$1.8 million.</p>
